      explanation: "The correct answer is Abdel Fattah El-Sisi. The chief guest at India's 74th Republic Day celebrations was Abdel Fattah El- Sisi, the President of Egypt. He was invited as a special guest to strengthen the bilateral ties between India and Egypt. This was his first visit to India since he took office in 2014. During his visit, several agreements were signed between the two countries in the areas of defence, trade, and culture. Francois Hollande is the former President of France and was the chief guest at India's Republic Day celebrations in 2016. Cyril Ramaphosa is the President of South Africa and was the chief guest at India's Republic Day celebrations in 2019. Jair Bolsonaro is the President of Brazil and was invited as a chief guest at India's Republic Day celebrations in 2020.",
